# LiNKtrend Ecosystem Master Rule

Cursor is the architecture and integration IDE for the LiNKtrend AI Agent Ecosystem. Codex, Antigravity, Gemini/Kimi, and other agents are bounded workers operating through `.ai-swarm/` work packets.

Repository files, Git history, `.ai-swarm/` documents, and committed implementation files are the source of truth. Do not rely on chat memory, IDE memory, or unstated assumptions.

Before coding, read in this order:

1. `.cursor/rules/`
2. `.cursor/skills/SKILLS_CATALOG.md`
3. `.ai-swarm/ARCHITECT_REVIEW_REPORT.md` if present
4. `docs/architecture/repo-architecture-target.md`
5. `docs/architecture/system-completion-targets.md`
6. `.ai-swarm/MASTER_PLAN.md`
7. `.ai-swarm/ARCHITECTURE_RULES.md`
8. `.ai-swarm/CONTRACTS_MVO.md`
9. `.ai-swarm/REPO_INVENTORY.md`
10. `.ai-swarm/DECISIONS.md`
11. the active `.ai-swarm/WORK_PACKETS/*.md`

Use `.cursor/skills/SKILLS_CATALOG.md` for progressive disclosure: select the skills, MCP servers, and plugin references relevant to the task before opening full skill bodies or tool descriptors. Do not bulk-load every skill file.

If these files do not exist, create `.ai-swarm/` first. Do not implement application code before the command center exists.

The first MVO is the LinkSites / WebsiteFactory lead-to-preview-site flow.

The development posture is reuse-first: inspect active and archived repos before creating new implementation.

New work must use the canonical post-cleanup folders: `LiNKaios/`, `LiNKbrain/`, `LiNKskills/`, `LiNKautowork/`, `LiNKbot/`, `LiNKguard/`, and `modules/`. Do not create new work under legacy `plugins/vertical` or moved `apps/*` runtime paths.

For module work, start in the module folder and maintain one canonical workflow map there. The module workflow map is the readable source of truth; other planes implement referenced parts through their own ownership folders.
